<title>UK: Liverpool cotton.</title>
<headline>Liverpool cotton.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The partial recovery of New York futures mostly had a dampening effect on European mill demand, brokers said.</p>
<p>With the Easter holiday imminent, few spinners showed any genuine desire to examine their raw material requirements afresh, especially in view of the rather firmer prices quoted today by most merchants.</p>
<p>A selective, price-testing enquiry was in evidence, pricipally for supplies available for second quarter shipment, but real buying interest was lacking.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
